What happens when this Python code runs?

```python
from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor

pool = ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1)

def inner():
    return 42

def outer():
    return pool.submit(inner).result()

print(pool.submit(outer).result())
```

Why does this Java code hang forever once a waiter is inside the inner `wait()`?

```java
// waiter
synchronized (outer) {
    synchronized (inner) {
        while (!ready) inner.wait();
    }
}
// notifier
synchronized (outer) {
    synchronized (inner) {
        ready = true;
        inner.notifyAll();
    }
}
```

This Java transfer orders locks by identity hash code. Under heavy load it still deadlocks very rarely. Why, and what is the textbook fix?

```java
int h1 = System.identityHashCode(from);
int h2 = System.identityHashCode(to);
if (h1 < h2) { synchronized (from) { synchronized (to) { move(); } } }
else         { synchronized (to)   { synchronized (from) { move(); } } }
```

A cache method holds a `ReentrantReadWriteLock` read lock and, on a miss, calls `rw.writeLock().lock()` to "upgrade". Only one thread is running. What happens?

```java
rw.readLock().lock();
try {
    if (!cache.containsKey(k)) {
        rw.writeLock().lock();
        try { cache.put(k, load(k)); } finally { rw.writeLock().unlock(); }
    }
} finally { rw.readLock().unlock(); }
```

Two classes from a taxi-dispatch system deadlock under load. What is the root cause, and what is the recommended refactoring?

```java
class Taxi {
    synchronized void setLocation(Point p) {
        location = p;
        if (p.equals(dest)) dispatcher.notifyAvailable(this);
    }
    synchronized Point getLocation() { return location; }
}
class Dispatcher {
    synchronized void notifyAvailable(Taxi t) { available.add(t); }
    synchronized Image getImage() {
        for (Taxi t : taxis) image.drawMarker(t.getLocation());
        return image;
    }
}
```
